     "function_name": "agent",
     "arguments": {
      "prompt": "I need to find the code responsible for displaying links in comments, specifically code that handles truncation of long links with '...' and the \"select text view\" feature. \n\nThe bug is: \"Long links in comments are truncated and end with '...'. Though in the select text view they are still truncated, this means if you select text it will not include the whole link.\"\n\nPlease search the codebase thoroughly for:\n1. Any code related to link detection, parsing, or display in comments/text\n2. Any truncation logic that adds '...' to links\n3. Code related to \"select text\" or text selection in comments\n4. TextView or EditText configurations that might truncate spans\n5. Any LinkMovementMethod, URLSpan, or hyperlink handling\n6. Files related to comments display, post display, or content rendering\n\nSearch patterns to try: \"truncate\", \"ellipsize\", \"LinkMovementMethod\", \"URLSpan\", \"Selectable\", \"select text\", \"comments\", \"link\", \"...\" in Java/Kotlin/Android files.\n\nReport all relevant files and code snippets you find.",
